  - 2026-07-07 TinyRustLM quality/UI-lock goal routed through `docs/report-intake/2026-07-07/tinyrustlm-quality-ui-lock-goal-2026-07-07.md`: the approved TinyRustLM.com look is locked by `tinyrustlm/tools/capture-ui-lock.js` and live desktop/mobile screenshot signatures. Source/native runtime applies bounded repetition penalty `4.25`; suppresses non-content specials, unsafe control bytes, early EOS, and repeated-token runs during generation; and fails closed with `generation failed: degenerate repeated output` plus `generation_stop_reason=quality_filter` instead of accepting `eeeee`-style fixture output. Model manifests now declare capability metadata (`tokenizer`, `tokenizer_checksum`, `context_length`, `output_contract`, `prompt_format`, `instruction_support`, `chat_support`, `quality_eval_status`, `intended_use`), and browser/native eval route visible prompts through manifest-declared prompt formats instead of browser-side answer templates. `tinyrustlm/runtime/src/eval_runner.rs` enforces the `honest-assistant-quality-v1` no-cheat lane across six fixed prompts plus six seeded holdout prompts (`holdout_seed=2026070801`), records fixed/holdout counts, per-case origin/runtime prompts/output format/required JSON keys/diagnostics, normalizes sidecar values as `none`, `not-applicable`, or `empty-output`, and rejects malformed JSON, missing JSON keys, repeated/empty/echo/low-diversity output, and fixture-boundary claims even when runtime generation returns an error. `tinyrustlm/tools/slm_pack/src/provenance.rs` binds prompt/capability metadata and includes holdout metadata/case origin in eval evidence checksums so holdout proof is not decorative. Rebuilt WASM manifest is `147405` bytes with runtime checksum `0xe31074a5c0b55ebc`, and `browser-smoke` single mode now expects the toy model to surface the fail-closed quality-filter error through the real UI transcript rather than pretending the fixture is assistant-quality. Regenerated `tiny-test-model-q8-honest.eval` and `t