  model_breeding_reference: wiki/runtime-mirust/research/model-breeding-reference-ideas-2026-06-26.md carries compatible merge, sparse-lineage, adapter-ecology including trained low-rank adapter source bundles, source-backed ALR1 manifests, source-backed browser ALR1 routes, source-backed ALR1 receipt source echoes, and ADP1/ASP1/ALR1, population-search, federated/local-update, browser-constrained-assembly, UAIX-memory-strategy, heritable-artifact, mate-selection, phenotype-evidence, and speciation-and-fit lanes.
  modelbreeder_zero_dependency_reference: wiki/runtime-mirust/research/modelbreeder-zero-dependency-reference-ideas-2026-06-28.md carries genome/fitness/novelty/population/speciation guidance plus Wasm SIMD, hierarchical quantization, deterministic tokenizer/sampler, KV-cache, allocator, multimodal, and telemetry lanes.
  model_breeding_concept_routes:
    - heritable artifacts: .slm files, manifests, adapter packages, module-plan receipts, assembly receipts, eval sidecars, selector entries, and Model Provenance Artifact rows.
    - mate selection: compatibility reports, population reviews, parent-pool recipes, relatedness checksums, seed weights, and objective vectors.
    - phenotype evidence: runtime-smoke sidecars, eval-case evidence checksums, Model Provenance rows, browser smokes, and promotion ledgers.
    - speciation and fit: f32/q8_0/q4_0 families, tokenizer families, tensor layouts, adapter families, and browser resource envelopes.
  latest_smollm2_gqa_gbpe_planning_report: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/smollm2-gqa-gbpe-planning-memory-2026-07-08.md records SmolLM2 GQA/GBPE support plus the served 360M q4 `.slm` quality evidence: native eval 12/12, eval case checksum `0xf63dee70df605f05`, browser `smollm2q4` assistant-quality smoke pass, and remaining broader product gaps.
  hot_synthesis: .uai/report-synthesis.uai
  long_term_pointer_ledger: .uai/long-term-memory.uai
  site_voice_route: .uai/taboo.uai keeps public copy on proof, craft, lineage, fit, local agency, routes, and implementation evidence.
active_next_steps:
  - 2026-07-10 deploy/verify next step for hosted browser memory: wire `tinyrustlm/deploy/memory-endpoints-relay-worker.js` to the production `tinyrustlm.com` route `/api/memoryendpoints/*`, then run `memory-endpoints-live` with browser base URL `/api/memoryendpoints` or add a dedicated live relay smoke to prove real short-term/status save+search, long-term/handoff save+search, `Web memory active`, hosted generation context, `tokenInLocalStorage=false`, no localStorage leaks, and no server model-byte proxying. Direct MemoryEndpoints CORS still needs service-side OPTIONS headers; keep `memory-endpoints-cors-ui` and `memory-endpoints-relay-ui` explicit-only regression modes.
  - 2026-07-10 next MemoryEndpoints hosted-memory step: wait for MemoryEndpoints.com service CORS fix, then rerun credentialed `eng/verify-tinyrustlm-ui.ps1 -BrowserSmokeModes memory-endpoints-live` and require redacted browser proof of short-term/status search, long-term/handoff search, `Web memory active`, hosted generation context, `tokenInLocalStorage=false`, no localStorage leaks, and no raw workspace id/key output. Keep the new `memory-endpoints-cors-ui` fake-host smoke as the regression for user-facing CORS/network-policy messaging and session-key non-persistence. Do not mark hosted browser memory complete while real `OPTIONS` preflight is still 401/no-CORS at MemoryEndpoints.com.
  - 2026-07-10 MemoryEndpoints hosted memory browser/live slice is active and public-contract aligned in TinyRustLM.com: Advanced Model Selection has opt-in MemoryEndpoints.com controls, persists only non-secret settings including auth-header mode and search tier, keeps the workspace key in page-session memory, supports both `Authorization: Bearer <WORKSPACE_KEY>` and `X-MemoryEndpoints-Key`, registers `tinyrustlm-agent`, maps TinyRustLM Save Short-Term/Save Long-Term to `/api/matm/memory-events/submit` with `scope=project`, `scopeId=tinyrustlm.com`, `actorAgentId`, `summary`, and `memoryType=status|handoff`, searches authenticated GET `/api/matm/search` with project filters and optional tier filters (`short_term -> memory_type=status`, `long_term -> memory_type=handoff`, all -> no memory_type), and injects only visible hosted search snippets into generation context. Verification passed: `node --check tinyrustlm/app/app.js`, `node --check tinyrustlm/tools/browser-smoke.js`, `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-memory-endpoints`, `dotnet test dotnet/tests/TinyRustLM.Core.Tests/TinyRustLM.Core.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter MemoryEndpoints`, browser-smoke `memory-endpoints-ui`, `dotnet test ... --filter ReportIntakeMemoryTests`, full optional package pack, PackageBoundaryTests, and live `eng/verify-memory-endpoints-live.ps1` against MemoryEndpoints.com. Live report now also proves meeting-room transcript coordination: `status_search_result_count=1`, `handoff_search_result_count=1`, short-term/status found, long-term/handoff found, no cross-tier marker leakage, `transcript_result_count=10`, `transcript_probe_found=true`, `transcript_items_shape=items`, `transcript_exposure_flags_clear=true`, and `secret_material_included=false`; report SHA256 `5BB0DCEABF6A3752D9AEE93CFDF9B30E3B46F5E314F649C38AB91C5DBB49114F`. Verifier hashes: PowerShell `48CFF73E485005B57839E8D7A46675116CB5B1DA15CBEBD2F345BF96FAB1307A`, Bash `F1D417B391429315109EE7EE77BEE4E87DE3363E4D3411FDACA58BC76CB305EE`. Preserve the no-hidden-upload rule: generation must not silently upload prompts, `.slm`, raw `.uai` files, or private logs.
  - 2026-07-10 MemoryEndpoints .NET meeting-room SDK slice added to `TinyRustLM.MemoryEndpoints`: `MemoryEndpointsRoutes.FromBaseUri` builds the public MATM routes, optional route properties cover meeting-room list/create/post/read/mark-read, and `TinyRustLmMemoryEndpointsClient` exposes public-safe `ListMeetingRoomsAsync`, `CreateMeetingRoomAsync`, `PostMeetingMessageAsync`, `ReadMeetingMessagesAsync`, typed `ReadMeetingTranscriptAsync`, and `MarkMeetingRoomReadAsync`. Created rooms are restricted to `goal` or `task`, listing can filter company/workspace/project/goal/task, all meeting summaries use `safeSummary`, transcript parsing normalizes the live `items` shape and fails closed on raw credential/payload exposure flags, routes fail closed when not configured, and token material stays out of payloads and diagnostics. Verification passed: `dotnet test dotnet/tests/TinyRustLM.Core.Tests/TinyRustLM.Core.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter MemoryEndpoints` (11/11), full PackageBoundaryTests (45/45), `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-memory-endpoints` (5/5), `bash -n eng/verify-memory-endpoints-live.sh`, PowerShell missing-credential verifier, live hosted verifier, targeted secret scan, and docs/package metadata update. Connector doc SHA256 `D34C1052E38E3EA10B5A7B3DBA4235F5A1D6A0B6C7778871B2A760B163324CB8`; client SHA256 `F818A881E78107623D84ACC5E09D030960BD2456ACA861CE90CC8822822F7144`; test SHA256 `9DAABE65282AC904A828F7A0F2A30CA2B26FE147F12AB72CD85A0EFC8998BE99`; package-boundary SHA256 `CF67F60E14052093EF285099D54B3F4250077BEC3FD3C0388E35835360055813`.
  - Preserve the 2026-07-10 assistant-quality JSON no-cheat boundary in tinyrustlm/runtime/src/eval_runner.rs: honest evals may expose structured JSON helpers, but if raw model-generated `status=` or `reason=` field evidence had to be repaired into a clean JSON value, `quality_failures` must include `json_raw_field_required_repair:<key>` and the case must not certify assistant quality. Verification: `cargo test -p tinyrustlm-runtime` passed with 165 unit tests plus 2 eval CLI tests after adding the raw-field repair gate.
